=== is it a signal, or a bet on which NAMES survived? ===
The permutation null cannot answer this. Permuting returns within a
date destroys the name-return link, so a book that is simply long
the same survivors every day earns ~0 under permutation and looks
significant. This project has the exact precedent: a cross-sectional
book built without the within-name check held NVDA on 100% of days
against SPY on 100% of days and 'returned' 34.9% a year.

